{
 "plan": {
  "title": "School Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Enrolment trends, infrastructure status, and gender gaps across schools",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Schools",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"School Code\") AS n FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Girls Enrolled",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Girls 2024\") AS n FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Boys Enrolled",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Boys 2024\") AS n FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Schools with Electricity",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"school_infrastructure\" WHERE \"Electricity\" = 'Yes'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Girls Enrolment by Year",
    "sql": "SELECT \"School Code\", SUM(\"Girls 2022\") AS g22, SUM(\"Girls 2023\") AS g23, SUM(\"Girls 2024\") AS g24 FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY g24 DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "g24",
    "y": [
     "g22",
     "g23",
     "g24"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Boys Enrolment by Year",
    "sql": "SELECT \"School Code\", SUM(\"Boys 2022\") AS b22, SUM(\"Boys 2023\") AS b23, SUM(\"Boys 2024\") AS b24 FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY b24 DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "b24",
    "y": [
     "b22",
     "b23",
     "b24"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "pie",
    "title": "Infrastructure Availability",
    "sql": "SELECT \"School Code\", SUM(CASE WHEN \"Electricity\" = 'Yes' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS has_elec, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Drinking water\" = 'Yes' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS has_water, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Toilets functional (girls)\" = 'Yes' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS has_toilets FROM \"school_infrastructure\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY has_elec DESC LIMIT 8",
    "x": "has_elec",
    "y": [
     "has_water",
     "has_toilets"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p8",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 10 Schools by Girls Enrolment",
    "sql": "SELECT \"School Name\", SUM(\"Girls 2024\") AS total_girls, SUM(\"Boys 2024\") AS total_boys FROM \"school_enrolment_by_year\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY total_girls DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard provides a snapshot of the educational landscape, focusing on enrolment figures and infrastructure quality. The top KPIs reveal the total number of schools, the aggregate count of girls and boys enrolled, and the proportion of schools equipped with electricity.\n\nThe bar charts illustrate the growth trajectory of enrolment for both genders over the last three years, allowing for a direct comparison of trends at the individual school level. The pie chart visualizes the availability of critical infrastructure, specifically electricity, drinking water, and functional toilets for girls, highlighting potential gaps in resource distribution.\n\nFinally, the table lists the top ten schools by girls' enrolment, providing a detailed view of the most successful institutions in terms of female participation. This data helps identify high-performing schools and areas where infrastructure investment might be most needed to support continued growth."
 },
